{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QuykurDZ1RhBbjn6so24w1","type":"tool_result","content":"01_cross_fitted_recalibrated_ppi_intervals/program_1/analysis:\nmetric_values.csv\nrun_summary.csv\ntimeseries.csv\n\n01_cross_fitted_recalibrated_ppi_intervals/program_1/src:\nharness.py\nprogram.py\n{\"combined_score\": 0.027080121099549548, \"controls_passed\": 1.0, \"coverage_min_family\": 0.9333333333333333, \"coverage_pooled\": 0.9433333333333334, \"log_ratio_vs_classical_mean\": 0.49413320035056846, \"log_ratio_vs_ppi_family_alphafold\": 0.010428103934328083, \"log_ratio_vs_ppi_family_forest\": 0.016791531451063855, \"log_ratio_vs_ppi_family_galaxies\": 0.0035018565908873267, \"log_ratio_vs_ppi_family_gene_expression\": 0.028990259989334164, \"log_ratio_vs_ppi_family_synthetic\": 0.07568885353213431, \"log_ratio_vs_ppi_lambda1_mean\": 0.05393618082192103, \"n_failed_episodes\": 0}\"\"\"Starter candidate: PPI++ (power-tuned prediction-powered) confidence interval for a mean.\n\nInterface: ``handle(request) -> response`` over finite JSON-compatible values\n(``python_rpc_v1:handle``). The candidate runs in an isolated process with no\nfilesystem or network access shared with the evaluator; all data arrive inline.\n\nTask. A fixed predictor, a small labeled sample and a larger unlabeled sample are given.\nReturn a confidence interval [lo, hi] for the population mean E[Y] at level 1 - alpha.\nNominal coverage must hold in repeated sampling; the score rewards narrower intervals than\nthe PPI++ interval (``ppi_py.ppi_mean_ci`` default power tuning) at maintained coverage.\nNo extra labels, no predictor change, no extra unlabeled data exist.\n\nOperations (every request is a dict with an ``\"op\"`` key):\n\n``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": int}``\n    Sent exactly once at the start of every episode (and the process may be restarted\n    first). Must clear ALL cross-episode state and seed only the candidate's own\n    randomness. Any non-negative integer seed is valid; the seed never selects a dataset,\n    plane or workload. Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": True}``.\n\n``{\"op\": \"estimate\", \"n\": int, \"N\": int, \"alpha\": float,\n   \"Y_labeled\": ARR, \"Yhat_labeled\": ARR, \"Yhat_unlabeled\": ARR}``\n    One independent labeled/unlabeled draw per episode (one estimate call per episode).\n    ``ARR`` is ``{\"dtype\": \"float64\", \"shape\": [length], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n    \"data\": <base64 of little-endian float64 bytes>}``. ``len(Y_labeled) ==\n    len(Yhat_labeled) == n`` and ``len(Yhat_unlabeled) == N``. All values are finite.\n    The labeled and unlabeled records are i.i.d. draws from one population; the labeled\n    Yhat are the predictor outputs on the labeled records. alpha is 0.05 in every plane.\n    Response: exactly ``{\"lo\": float, \"hi\": float}`` (finite, lo <= hi); no other keys\n    are allowed. A malformed, non-finite, reversed or late response counts as a miss\n    with a worst-case width (10x the classical interval).\n    Per-call wall deadline: 3 seconds (enforced). Keep BLAS threads at 1.\n    The dataset or family name, population truth, baseline outputs and scores are never\n    sent. Requests of up to N = 20000 unlabeled and n = 500 labeled records occur\n    (about 225 KB base64 per request).\n\nAny other op, or an estimate before reset, is an error.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport base64\nimport math\nimport os\nfrom statistics import NormalDist\n\nos.environ.setdefault(\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", \"1\")\nos.environ.setdefault(\"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\", \"1\")\nos.environ.setdefault(\"MKL_NUM_THREADS\", \"1\")\n\nimport numpy as np  # noqa: E402\n\n_STATE = {\"ready\": False, \"seed\": None, \"rng\": None}\n\n\ndef _decode(arr, name):\n    if (type(arr) is not dict or arr.get(\"dtype\") != \"float64\"\n            or arr.get(\"encoding\") != \"base64-le\" or type(arr.get(\"data\")) is not str):\n        raise ValueError(f\"bad array {name}\")\n    raw = base64.b64decode(arr[\"data\"].encode(\"ascii\"), validate=True)\n    out = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype=\"<f8\").astype(np.float64)\n    if list(arr.get(\"shape\", [])) != [out.size] or not np.all(np.isfinite(out)):\n54:def _decode(arr, name):\n65:def classical_ci(y, alpha):\n71:def ppi_pp_ci(y, yhat, yhat_unl, alpha):\n87:def ppi_plus_plus_mean_ci(y, yhat, yhat_unl, alpha):\n92:def ppi_mean_ci(y, yhat, yhat_unl, alpha):\n101:def _t_crit(alpha, df):\n120:def _pav(x, y):\n142:def _fit_isotonic(x, y):\n156:def _fit_binned(x, y, n_bins):\n167:def _folds(n, k, seed):\n176:def _cross_fit(y, yhat, yhat_unl, fitter, k, seed):\n188:def _control_variate_ci(y, f_lab, f_unl, alpha, extra_df=0):\n215:def crppi_mean_ci(y, yhat, yhat_unl, alpha, method=\"isotonic\", k=5, seed=0):\n236:def stratified_ppi_mean_ci(y, yhat, yhat_unl, alpha, n_bins=5):\n260:def _best_interval(y, yhat, yhat_unl, alpha, seed):\n281:def _estimate(request):\n295:def handle(request):\n{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"With labeled set, unlabeled set and predictor all fixed, the PPI++ interval for a mean (a single scalar power-tuning weight on the raw prediction) is not the shortest valid interval. The labeled data can be used to learn a cross-fitted recalibration g(Yhat) ~ E[Y|Yhat] (isotonic, quantile-binned/stratified, or monotone spline). Plugging g into the PPI estimator, mean_unlabeled g + mean_labeled (Y - g), with a shrinkage weight toward the classical estimator, should give valid (>=95% empirical coverage within Monte Carlo error) and shorter intervals than PPI/PPI++ whenever the predictor is nonlinearly miscalibrated (conditional-mean curve far from linear in Yhat) and n is moderate-to-large (about >=200). Predicted gain: the asymptotic variance reduction equals the drop in residual variance Var(Y-lambda*Yhat) -> Var(Y-E[Y|Yhat]), a bound that can be computed from data. When Yhat is already near-linearly calibrated, when n is very small (<~50, where cross-fitting noise and Wald undercoverage dominate), or when Yhat is nearly uninformative, we predict zero or negative gain relative to PPI++ and possible undercoverage. The study maps the gain/no-gain regimes on 9 real ppi-python datasets plus known-truth synthetic data, and checks the width-ratio theory against experiments.\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"cycle01_crppi_mean_ci\",\n  \"implementation_plan\": [\n    \"Follow the entrypoint/interface of the existing baseline program (src/program.py); put the estimators in a pure-numpy/scipy/sklearn module under src/ and keep it CPU-only and seeded.\",\n    \"Target: population mean of Y (secondary: a quantile, and OLS coefficient on census_* if time allows). Justify: mean is the cleanest case where the semiparametric efficiency bound is explicit.\",\n    \"Baselines: classical Wald/t interval on labeled data only; PPI (lambda=1); PPI++ with data-driven scalar lambda; stratified PPI with quantile bins of Yhat; (if available) ppi_py==0.2.3 reference to check own implementation matches within tolerance.\",\n    \"Proposed methods: cross-fitted g via K-fold (K=5-10) isotonic regression, quantile-binned means (B chosen by cross-validated residual variance), and monotone/low-order spline; estimate per-fold g on labeled folds, apply to held-out labeled fold and to all unlabeled points (average over folds); estimator = mean_unl g + mean_lab (Y-g) with variance estimated from the cross-fit residuals (plus the unlabeled-term variance); optional shrinkage lambda in [0,1] between classical and recalibrated estimator chosen by variance estimate.\",\n    \"Small-n variants: Student-t critical value with n-1 df, and a bootstrap-t / percentile bootstrap over labeled and unlabeled points jointly; compare coverage and width.\",\n    \"Experiment A (real data): for each of galaxies, forest, alphafold (3 indicators), gene_expression, census_income, census_healthcare, census_education, plankton, ballots as applicable, treat full-data mean of Y as truth (for plankton/ballots use only pooled labeled data or the labeled year as truth a